From: HarmonyOS PC Porting <porting@example.com>
Date: Mon, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix generate_interceptors to recognize OHOS platform

The generate_interceptors Python script checks sys.platform to
determine the target platform. On HarmonyOS PC, Python reports
sys.platform as 'ohos' (not 'linux'), even though the underlying
kernel is Linux and the intercepted functions are identical.

Add 'ohos' to the supported platforms list and map it to 'linux'
target, since OHOS uses Linux-compatible syscall semantics.

This is a build-time code generation script, not a runtime component.

--- a/src/interceptor/generate_interceptors
+++ b/src/interceptor/generate_interceptors
@@ -26,8 +26,8 @@
   exit(1)
 outdir = sys.argv[1]
 
-supported_platforms = ['linux', 'darwin']
-if sys.platform.startswith('linux'):
+supported_platforms = ['linux', 'darwin', 'ohos']
+if sys.platform.startswith('linux') or sys.platform.startswith('ohos'):
   target = "linux"
 elif sys.platform.startswith('darwin'):
   target = "darwin"
